# KNIRVORACLE SDK Tool - CLI Development Plan

## Overview

This document outlines the comprehensive development plan for the KNIRVORACLE command-line interface (CLI) tool. The tool will enable developers to interact with the KNIRVORACLE blockchain, manage wallets, and register capabilities through multiple integration routes. It serves as a critical interface between developers and the KNIRVORACLE ecosystem, allowing for seamless integration of custom plugins, MCP servers, and operational procedures.

The CLI tool will be built using Go, the Cobra CLI framework, and the Bubbletea terminal UI library, providing a robust, user-friendly interface with comprehensive documentation and error handling. It will support all core KNIRVORACLE operations, with a particular focus on secure wallet management and capability registration through both direct plugin implementation and MCP server integration via extrapolation and interpolation routes. The Bubbletea framework will enable rich interactive terminal experiences with customizable themes, responsive layouts, and intuitive navigation.

